.TH CW "1" "October 2026" "cw 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cw \- cw windows
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cw
\fI\,windows \/\fR[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR] [\fI\,NAME\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IP
Show windows belonging to a Context, or all iTerm windows.
.IP
Modes:
.TP
cw windows
current Context (auto\-detected)
.TP
cw windows MyProject
specific Context
.TP
cw windows \fB\-\-all\fR
ALL iTerm windows (tracked + untracked)
.TP
cw windows \fB\-\-untracked\fR
only windows NOT in any Context
.IP
Detail levels:
.TP
(default)
windows only
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
windows + tabs
.TP
\fB\-vv\fR
windows + tabs + panes with CWDs
.IP
With \fB\-\-all\fR/\-\-untracked, each window shows a ref number (#1, #2, ...)
that you can use with `cw join` to add it to a Context:
.IP
cw join MyProject 3
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Detail level: \fB\-v\fR shows tabs, \fB\-vv\fR shows tabs+panes with CWDs.
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Show ALL iTerm windows with Context info.
.TP
\fB\-\-untracked\fR
Show only windows NOT belonging to any Context.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show this message and exit.
